## Delivered boundary

Trusted bounded worker, pinned inputs/results, numerical clock, one writer, native DC/RC reference run, probes and failure states on a standalone electronic root.

## Ownership and possible overlap

Shared numerical job/clock/result/authority services plus the first circuit adapter. Other solver integrations wait for this tested handoff.

Independent ready packages may proceed together only after file/service ownership is reserved. Use separate leaf modules or isolated checkouts; shared migrations, command schemas, source/selection types, renderer lifetimes, runtime scheduling and performance sessions have one owner at a time. If actual code inspection finds an unproved shared boundary, add a dependency or serialize that work before coding. No promised worker count follows from the graph.

## Ordered work

Follow this package's task order. Original identifiers remain traceable; a reference to another former stage means its needed published contract, not an implicit global sequence. All native interaction, backend/persistence, authority, correctness and applicable resource obligations remain included.

### Task 15a.T01

- [ ] **15a.T01.** Freeze B44 equations/models, numerical ranges, reference outputs, interface assumptions, transition pairs and quantitative limits. Evaluate an established circuit evaluator against the bounded fixture before selecting it; ngspice is prior art/candidate, not an already chosen dependency. Audit licensing, supported platforms, cancellation, input limits and worker isolation. Do not implement a general circuit solver solely to avoid a small adapter.

### Task 15a.T02

- [ ] **15a.T02.** Extend shared activity/jobs with captured composition/netlist/model versions, initial conditions, numerical settings, clock, admitted resources, result mapping, cancellation and one fenced execution authority. Implement a bounded worker boundary and basic native Run/Pause/Step/Reset, source/probe selection and time plots. Install no evaluator or execute imported code merely on opening a device.

### Task 15a.T03

- [ ] **15a.T03.** Translate the supported source graph to the evaluator with verified terminal/element mappings, units/signs and explicit initialization. Detect unsupported models, missing reference, singular networks and failed/nonconverged steps. Complete independent DC and RC transient references before adding the nonlinear switch/diode example. Failed output remains inspectable with status, never a passed current solution.

